dsh-shared-bash README · Tools：Every tool takes an optional `session_id`. Omitted, it means "the calling agent's own session"; passed, it means "that session's terminal", which is the explicit cross-agent sharing this plugin offers:

```text
bash_list              → 3f2a… · busy · C:\proj\widgets
bash_read   {session_id: "3f2a…"}
bash_exec   {session_id: "3f2a…", command: "git status --short"}
bash_wait   {job_id: "bash-9c1e…"}
